    <briefdescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="class_mutable_engine_object" kindref="compound">MutableEngineObject</ref></computeroutput> wrapper holding a raw <computeroutput>SLEvaluator*</computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Stores a raw pointer rather than <computeroutput>unique_ptr</computeroutput> <mdash/> per the inline comment, this is a deliberate leak that avoids a heap-corruption bug triggered when ownership is transferred. <computeroutput><ref refid="class_m2_s_l_evaluator_a948a2db6aa407dfb5555d616387e7e15_1a948a2db6aa407dfb5555d616387e7e15" kindref="member">value()</ref></computeroutput> returns the underlying abstract evaluator for engine code that needs to call <computeroutput>evaluate</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>specialize</computeroutput> directly. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
